content:
{
  "asset": "Pump P-101 — AquaDyne HF-300, serial HF3-22120, filtered-water line; dry ran for approximately 15 minutes during tank changeover and is now primed and running.",
  "priority": "P2",
  "stop_equipment_now": false,
  "condition_assessment": [
    {
      "statement": "Vibration 3.0 mm/s: on the HF-300 Figure 3 bearing-housing vibration-velocity scale, this falls within Zone B (2.8–4.5 mm/s RMS), labelled 'Long-term operation'. It is above the 2.8 mm/s Zone A/B boundary but below the 4.5 mm/s Zone C boundary; Zone C is restricted operation requiring planned maintenance, and Zone D (7.1–11.0 mm/s shown) is 'Damage likely — stop the pump'. Thus the reported value does not meet the immediate-stop criterion. The assessment assumes the report's value is vibration velocity RMS on a bearing housing; that measurement basis must be confirmed, and both housings must be checked with the highest reading classified.",
      "citations": [
        "C06",
        "C07",
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Housing temperature 69 C: the applicable HF-300 limits are normal up to 70 C, alarm at 80 C and trip at 90 C. The reading is therefore within the documented normal range, 11 C below alarm and 21 C below trip. It does not meet the site requirement for a priority-1 work order, which applies when bearing temperature is above the manufacturer's alarm limit. The manual specifies housing-surface temperature measurement; the report does not confirm the measurement point.",
      "citations": [
        "C01",
        "C02",
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Dry-run exposure: the manual specifies Plan 11 seal flush from pump discharge and says 'never run dry', so the approximately 15-minute dry run was outside the operating instruction. No allowable dry-run duration is provided. No shaft-seal leakage has been seen yet, so leakage is not a confirmed symptom; however, a seal run dry and worn or cracked seal faces are documented causes of shaft-seal leakage.",
      "citations": [
        "C02",
        "C09"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Neither documented emergency criterion is met by the current readings: vibration is not in the highest severity zone and temperature is not above the 80 C alarm. P2 planned seal inspection is therefore appropriate for the dry-run excursion rather than an emergency stop or a temperature-driven P1. This does not establish that the seal is undamaged.",
      "citations": [
        "C02",
        "C07",
        "C09",
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "The current readings do not, by themselves, establish bearing wear, misalignment, impeller damage or cavitation. Those are troubleshooting possibilities for high vibration, while bearing replacement is required as a pair when either bearing shows wear, noise or high temperature; none of those findings is documented in the report.",
      "citations": [
        "C07",
        "C09",
        "C10"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "probable_causes": [
    {
      "statement": "Primary concern: possible mechanical-seal face damage from the known 15-minute dry run. This is a risk requiring inspection, not a confirmed failure, because the pump is now primed and no leakage has yet been observed.",
      "citations": [
        "C02",
        "C09"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "If leakage or seal damage is confirmed, worn or cracked seal faces and shaft misalignment are additional documented contributors to investigate. No seal-face examination or alignment measurement is available to rank these above the known dry-run exposure.",
      "citations": [
        "C09",
        "C10"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "tasks": [
    {
      "statement": "Before intrusive work, inspect for shaft-seal leakage and obtain a current baseline: measure vibration velocity on both bearing housings, classify the highest reading using Figure 3, and record bearing-housing surface temperature. Continue the manual's weekly two-housing vibration measurements after return to service.",
      "citations": [
        "C01",
        "C06",
        "C07",
        "C09"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "At the planned outage, isolate and drain the pump for seal inspection. Use the back pull-out arrangement, which permits rotating-assembly removal without disturbing the casing or pipework. The assembly weighs 68 kg, so use the required controlled lift.",
      "citations": [
        "C01",
        "C02",
        "C10",
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Remove the back pull-out assembly, impeller nut and impeller; withdraw the seal and sleeve. Inspect the sleeve for scoring and examine the seal for wear, cracking or other evidence consistent with dry running. Record whether leakage or internal damage is actually present before authorising seal replacement.",
      "citations": [
        "C09",
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "If seal replacement is required, fit cartridge seal HF3-450B, not HF3-450, together with a new HF3-120 casing gasket. HF3-450B is pre-set, so no sleeve measurement is needed for seal setting. Inspect the sleeve nevertheless and replace HF3-455 if scoring exceeds 0.1 mm depth. Fit a new casing gasket whenever the casing is opened, even if the seal is not replaced.",
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C10",
        "C13"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "On reassembly, follow the seal-replacement sequence and tighten all fasteners. Table 5 values are for lightly oiled threads: M24 impeller nut 160 Nm; M16 casing bolts 210 Nm; and M12 bearing-housing bolts 85 Nm if disturbed. For the HF3-450B seal gland nuts, use 30 Nm rather than the manual's superseded 25 Nm value.",
      "citations": [
        "C10",
        "C11",
        "C13"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Check shaft alignment when leakage troubleshooting requires it, and use a laser alignment tool after any work that moves the motor or bearing housing. Acceptance tolerances are parallel offset 0.05 mm and angular misalignment 0.05 mm per 100 mm.",
      "citations": [
        "C09",
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Do not replace bearings solely because of the reported 3.0 mm/s and 69 C readings. If inspection or subsequent operation establishes wear, noise or high temperature in either bearing, replace both bearings as a pair and revise the parts and labour scope accordingly.",
      "citations": [
        "C02",
        "C07",
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Before return to service, confirm the pump is primed and the documented Plan 11 flush arrangement from pump discharge is in service; do not run the pump dry. After reassembly, check for seal leakage and repeat the vibration and housing-temperature checks.",
      "citations": [
        "C01",
        "C02",
        "C06",
        "C09"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "parts": [
    {
      "part_number": "HF3-450B",
      "description": "Cartridge mechanical seal; quantity 1 if inspection authorises seal replacement. Mandatory substitute for HF3-450 on this serial-numbered pump; pre-set, with no sleeve measurement needed for seal setting.",
      "quantity": 1,
      "citations": [
        "C13"
      ]
    },
    {
      "part_number": "HF3-120",
      "description": "Casing gasket; quantity 1 for the planned opening. Replace whenever the casing is opened and when fitting a new seal.",
      "quantity": 1,
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "part_number": "HF3-455",
      "description": "Shaft sleeve; quantity 1 only if inspection finds scoring exceeding 0.1 mm depth.",
      "quantity": 1,
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C13"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "safety_controls": [
    {
      "statement": "For any work inside the pump or on its seal, apply electrical isolation and lock-out/tag-out at the MCC, mechanically isolate suction and discharge valves, and obtain a line-break permit after draining and venting. The manual procedure also requires the pump to be isolated and drained before seal work.",
      "citations": [
        "C10",
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "The 68 kg back pull-out assembly exceeds the site's 25 kg lifting threshold. Use a lifting plan signed by the shift supervisor and certified lifting equipment; the manual also expressly requires lifting equipment for this assembly.",
      "citations": [
        "C02",
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "If the filtered-water line is chemically dosed, wear chemical goggles and nitrile gloves. Dosing status must be confirmed before work.",
      "citations": [
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "If vibration reaches the manufacturer's highest severity zone, Zone D, stop the pump immediately and notify the reliability engineer before restart. The present 3.0 mm/s reading is Zone B and does not activate this control.",
      "citations": [
        "C07",
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "If bearing-housing temperature rises above the manufacturer's 80 C alarm limit, raise a priority-1 work order within the shift. The documented trip limit is 90 C; the current 69 C reading activates neither response.",
      "citations": [
        "C02",
        "C15"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "labour": [
    {
      "statement": "Conditional on seal replacement being authorised: mechanical-seal replacement standard labour is 4.0 hours with 2 technicians.",
      "citations": [
        "C12"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Conditional on laser alignment being required: allow 1.5 hours with 1 technician. Alignment is mandatory after work that moves the motor or bearing housing.",
      "citations": [
        "C10",
        "C12"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Bearing replacement is not included in the base labour scope. If wear, noise or high temperature is subsequently established, the standard for replacing the pair is 6.0 hours with 2 technicians.",
      "citations": [
        "C10",
        "C12"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "source_conflicts": [
    {
      "statement": "Seal part conflict: the manual parts list identifies component seal HF3-450, but Service Bulletin SB-2026-014, issued 14 March 2026, prohibits HF3-450 on HF-300 pumps from serial HF3-22000 upward and requires pre-set cartridge seal HF3-450B. P-101 is serial HF3-22120 and is therefore within the bulletin range; use HF3-450B for new work under this work order. The bulletin also controls this pump's sleeve-scoring rejection limit of greater than 0.1 mm.",
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C13"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Seal-gland torque conflict: manual Table 5 gives 25 Nm for M10 seal gland nuts, while SB-2026-014 specifies 30 Nm for HF3-450B. Because P-101 is within the bulletin's serial range, 30 Nm applies when HF3-450B is installed; the manual's 25 Nm value remains applicable only to pumps below HF3-22000 using HF3-450. Other relevant Table 5 torques remain 210 Nm for casing bolts, 160 Nm for the impeller nut and 85 Nm for bearing-housing bolts.",
      "citations": [
        "C11",
        "C13"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "open_questions": [
    "Was the 3.0 mm/s reading measured as vibration velocity RMS on a bearing housing, which housing was measured, and what is the reading on the other housing? C06 and C07 require this measurement basis and classification of the highest reading.",
    "Was 69 C measured on the bearing-housing surface, and at which bearing housing? The report does not provide the measurement point required for direct comparison with the manual's convention in C01.",
    "Has any shaft-seal leakage developed since the report, and do internal inspection findings show cracked or worn seal faces or sleeve scoring deeper than 0.1 mm? The evidence does not establish that seal or sleeve replacement is already necessary, nor does it prescribe automatic seal replacement after every dry run without leakage (C09, C10, C13).",
    "Is the filtered-water line chemically dosed? This determines whether chemical goggles and nitrile gloves are mandatory under C15.",
    "What caused the loss of prime during tank changeover, was the Plan 11 flush path available, and what operating or procedural change will prevent recurrence? The evidence contains no tank-changeover procedure, flush-line field inspection or root-cause analysis.",
    "Table 6 provides no standard labour time for the initial condition checks, inspection-only disassembly or reassembly without seal replacement; those durations require site estimation if they are to be scheduled separately (C12).",
    "Site definitions distinguishing P2 from P3 are not supplied. P2 is a planning judgement based on the prohibited dry-run exposure and the need for planned inspection, while recognising that neither documented emergency/P1 trigger is currently met."
  ]
}
